IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Articles 1 to 3.
-- LAYER 1: scope (Arts 1 and 3) and the definitions of Article 2. Written from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
--
-- A DIRECTIVE BINDS MEMBER STATES, NOT PEOPLE. Where the text says "Member States shall ensure that ..." a rule here
-- answers what the Directive REQUIRES the national law to give or impose; it does not answer what any one Member
-- State's transposing law says, or whether a provision has direct effect (NOTES.md, "Seat").
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words;
-- NOTHING = not covered (the text is silent, lists without closing, points outside the sources, or limits its own wording).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Articles 1 to 3 -- scope and definitions`

§§ `Article 1 -- scope and aim`

-- Art 1(1) is the statement of the aim of the Directive and creates no rule: inert (reason 1) in NOTES.md.

-- src:21 | The provisions of this Directive particularise and complement Directive 95/46/EC for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 1.
@ref Art 1(2) first sentence (src:21) row:A1(2).s1
GIVEN `the matter is the processing of personal data in the electronic communication sector, for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 1(2) the Directive particularises and complements Directive 95/46/EC on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the processing of personal data in the electronic communication sector, for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of the purposes mentioned in paragraph 1 (FORK F5: Directive 95/46/EC as printed)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:21 | Moreover, they provide for protection of the legitimate interests of subscribers who are legal persons.
@ref Art 1(2) second sentence (src:21) row:A1(2).s2
GIVEN `the subscriber is a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 1(2) the Directive provides for protection of the subscriber's legitimate interests` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber is a legal person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names subscribers who are legal persons and is silent on others
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:22 | This Directive shall not apply to activities which fall outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community, such as those covered by Titles V and VI of the Treaty on European Union, and in any case to activities concerning public security, defence, State security (including the economic well-being of the State when the activities relate to State security matters) and the activities of the State in areas of criminal law.
@ref Art 1(3) (src:22) row:A1(3)
GIVEN `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity concerns public security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity concerns defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity concerns State security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity relates to State security matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not apply to activities which fall outside the scope of the Treaty"
        IF `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any case to activities concerning public security, defence, State security"
        IF `the activity concerns public security` OR `the activity concerns defence` OR `the activity concerns State security` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "including the economic well-being of the State when the activities relate to State security matters" -- FORK F22: the "when" limb is read as limiting the economic well-being of the State only
        IF `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` AND `the activity relates to State security matters` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the activities of the State in areas of criminal law"
        IF `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence excludes; whether the Directive applies to anything else is Article 3's question
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Article 2 -- definitions`

-- Art 2 chapeau: the definitions of Directive 95/46/EC and Directive 2002/21/EC are borrowed. Neither is among the sources,
-- so whether a term is defined there is a fact the person states. See the fork register (NOTES.md, F1).
-- src:25 | Save as otherwise provided, the definitions in Directive 95/46/EC and in Directive 2002/21/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 7 March 2002 on a common regulatory framework for electronic communications networks and services (Framework Directive)
-- src:27 | shall apply.
@ref Art 2 chapeau (src:25-27) row:A2.borrowed
GIVEN `the term is defined in Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term is defined in Directive 2002/21/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Directive otherwise provides for the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2 the borrowed definition of the term applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Save as otherwise provided"
        IF `this Directive otherwise provides for the term` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the term is defined in Directive 95/46/EC` OR `the term is defined in Directive 2002/21/EC` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the borrowed definitions are in instruments that are not among the sources (FORK F1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Whether the terms of Directive 2002/21/EC now read as the terms of Directive (EU) 2018/1972 is not decided here.
-- The consolidated text of 2009 still names Directive 2002/21/EC; that the Publications Office lists Directive (EU) 2018/1972
-- as repealing it was checked against the Publications Office data on 2026-11-17 (NOTES.md, F2). NOT decided, and the later instrument is not imported (F2).
-- src:25 | Save as otherwise provided, the definitions in Directive 95/46/EC and in Directive 2002/21/EC
@ref Art 2 chapeau (src:25) row:A2.borrowed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2 the reference to Directive 2002/21/EC reads as a reference to the instrument that repealed it` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the repeal and what replaced Directive 2002/21/EC are not in the consolidated text (FORK F2: the repeal checked against the Publications Office data on 2026-11-17)
    NOTHING

-- The defined-term table: which paragraph of Article 2 defines each term. A term used without a definition of its own
-- in this text is not answered: its definition is in Directive 95/46/EC or Directive 2002/21/EC.
-- src:28 | The following definitions shall also apply:
@ref Art 2 lead-in (src:28) row:A2.own
GIVEN term IS A `Directive term`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Art 2 the paragraph of this Directive that defines the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `user` THEN JUST "Art 2(a)"
    WHEN `traffic data` THEN JUST "Art 2(b)"
    WHEN `location data` THEN JUST "Art 2(c)"
    WHEN `communication` THEN JUST "Art 2(d)"
    WHEN `consent` THEN JUST "Art 2(f)"
    WHEN `value added service` THEN JUST "Art 2(g)"
    WHEN `electronic mail` THEN JUST "Art 2(h)"
    WHEN `personal data breach` THEN JUST "Art 2(i)"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): used by this Directive but defined in Directive 95/46/EC or Directive 2002/21/EC (FORK F1)
    WHEN `subscriber` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): defined in Directive 95/46/EC
    WHEN `personal data` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): defined in Directive 95/46/EC
    WHEN `data subject` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): defined in Directive 2002/21/EC
    WHEN `publicly available electronic communications service` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): defined in Directive 2002/21/EC
    WHEN `public communications network` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): defined in Directive 2002/21/EC or elsewhere, not in this text
    WHEN `terminal equipment` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): neither defined in this text nor named as borrowed
    WHEN `direct marketing` THEN NOTHING

-- src:29 | ‘user’ means any natural person using a publicly available electronic communications service, for private or business purposes, without necessarily having subscribed to this service;
@ref Art 2(a) (src:29) row:A2(a)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(a) the person is a user` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person` AND `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service`
    -- Private or business purposes, subscribed or not: the text makes neither a condition.
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘user’ means any natural person using a publicly available electronic communications service"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:30 | ‘traffic data’ means any data processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network or for the billing thereof;
@ref Art 2(b) (src:30) row:A2(b)
GIVEN `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is processed for the billing of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(b) the data is traffic data` MEANS
    IF `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` OR `the data is processed for the billing of a communication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘traffic data’ means any data processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:32 | ‘location data’ means any data processed in an electronic communications network or by an electronic communications service, indicating the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service;
@ref Art 2(c) (src:32) row:A2(c)
GIVEN `the data is processed in an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is processed by an electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data indicates the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(c) the data is location data` MEANS
    IF (`the data is processed in an electronic communications network` OR `the data is processed by an electronic communications service`)
       AND `the data indicates the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘location data’ means any data processed in an electronic communications network or by an electronic communications service"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:34 | ‘communication’ means any information exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties by means of a publicly available electronic communications service.
@ref Art 2(d) first sentence (src:34) row:A2(d).s1
GIVEN `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(d) the information is a communication` MEANS
    IF `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` AND `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘communication’ means any information exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:34 | This does not include any information conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public over an electronic communications network except to the extent that the information can be related to the identifiable subscriber or user receiving the information;
@ref Art 2(d) second sentence (src:34) row:A2(d).s2
GIVEN `the information is conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public over an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information can be related to the identifiable subscriber or user receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(d) second sentence the information is a communication` MEANS
    IF `the information is conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public over an electronic communications network` AND (NOT `the information can be related to the identifiable subscriber or user receiving it`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not include any information conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): not broadcast, or broadcast but related to the identifiable subscriber or user "except to the extent": this sentence does not itself say the information is a communication (first sentence decides)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Art 2(e): ▼M2 DELETED, no text. Repealed or blank in this text (NOTES.md).

-- src:38 | ‘consent’ by a user or subscriber corresponds to the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC;
@ref Art 2(f) (src:38) row:A2(f)
GIVEN `the act of the user or subscriber is the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(f) the act of the user or subscriber is consent` MEANS
    IF `the act of the user or subscriber is the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘consent’ by a user or subscriber corresponds to the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC" -- FORK F3: "corresponds to" is read as "means"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:39 | ‘value added service’ means any service which requires the processing of traffic data or location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof;
@ref Art 2(g) (src:39) row:A2(g)
GIVEN `the service requires the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service requires the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(g) the service is a value added service` MEANS
    IF `the service requires the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof`
       OR `the service requires the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘value added service’ means any service which requires the processing of traffic data or location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:40 | ‘electronic mail’ means any text, voice, sound or image message sent over a public communications network which can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient;
@ref Art 2(h) (src:40) row:A2(h)
GIVEN `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` MEANS
    IF `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message`
       AND `the message is sent over a public communications network`
       AND `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘electronic mail’ means any text, voice, sound or image message sent over a public communications network"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:42 | ‘personal data breach’ means a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community.
@ref Art 2(i) (src:42) row:A2(i)
GIVEN `the event is a breach of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` MEANS
    IF `the event is a breach of security`
       AND (   `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data`
            OR `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data`
            OR `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data`
            OR `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data`
            OR `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data`)
       AND `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "‘personal data breach’ means a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Article 3 -- services concerned`

-- src:46 | This Directive shall apply to the processing of personal data in connection with the provision of publicly available electronic communications services in public communications networks in the Community, including public communications networks supporting data collection and identification devices.
@ref Art 3 (src:46) row:A3
GIVEN `the processing is of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the network is in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` MEANS
    IF `the processing is of personal data`
       AND `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service`
       AND `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices`
       AND `the network is in the Community`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall apply to the processing of personal data in connection with ..." carries no "only", so a case outside it is not answered
    ELSE NOTHING
